Z||000000||Gold-86SE||12-27-2001||03:55 PM||||<BR>I am attempting to determine the situation with the headlights on my 84.  I purchased the Fiero in early 2000, but this is the first time I have looked into the headlight situation.<P>Here is the deal.  The motors appear to work properly to lower the headlights, yet when I turn on the headlights... nada, zip, zero. The headlights shine bright, but the motors do not even turn.<P>Question is, is there a relay or something that controls the up motion of the headlight motor?  What am I missing?<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||REDHOTT88||12-27-2001||04:10 PM|||| A couple of helpful sites..<P> <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/headlights.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/headlights.html</A> <P> <A HREF="http://www.euronet.nl/users/fo_elmo/headlightact.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.euronet.nl/users/fo_elmo/headlightact.htm</A> <P>------------------<BR>                                                                                                         <BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/smilie/FIREdevil.gif">     <FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> <B>1988 Formula 2.8L V6</B> 5 speed Getrag </FONT><BR>            <I><FONT SIZE="1">(Runs smooth, shifts crisp, goes fast, red and shiny all over!)</FONT></I>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gold-86SE||12-27-2001||05:08 PM||||<BR>I would like to add, that it appears that the left headlight motor is attempting to run in an up manner, meaning trying to raise the light.  The motor is very warm to the touch, and I saw the crank bump as if to turn, but that is all it is doing.<P>Any ideas.||||reg||1
